# Every image in this repo builds from the *root*: two of them have to, because
# the uv workspace and the pub workspace both resolve from here, and a build
# context that starts inside one app cannot see the packages it depends on. So
# this file matters more than usual — without it the context is the whole tree,
# node_modules and .dart_tool included.

.git/
.github/

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
**/*.egg-info/

# ── Node ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
# Nuxt's working directories: regenerated inside the image, and copying a
# host-built `.output` in would ship whatever was last built on somebody's
# laptop rather than what the Dockerfile just produced.
**/.nuxt/
**/.output/

# ── Dart / Flutter ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/.dart_tool/
**/build/
# ...except the one build output an image actually packages. `apps/tv/Dockerfile`
# says why it takes a bundle rather than producing one.
!apps/tv/build/web/
**/.flutter-plugins
**/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
# Points at one machine's SDK. Baking it in makes a build that only works there.
apps/tv/android/local.properties

# ── Editors, OS, secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
**/.DS_Store
**/.env
**/.env.local
*.iml

# ── Things no image ever needs ───────────────────────────────────────────────
tools/

# Markdown is deliberately NOT excluded. Every Python package here declares
# `readme = "README.md"`, and hatchling refuses to build a wheel when the file
# the metadata names is missing — so dropping them turns a docs tidy-up into a
# failed image build.
